the A to Z of isms minimalism for some  people minimalism just means not owning  any staff it's a lifestyle choice it  means owning few possessions living in  largely empty space and even eating  minimalist food no chips for the  minimalists they own shiny white tablets  shop at little gray stores and don't  have enough black plastic chairs the sum  it's to do with architecture and for  others it's a musical movement in fact  minimalism is a philosophy with roots  and branches in many places the word  minimalism first turns up in 1965 in an  article by British philosopher Richard  Walheim who wrote about artists with  minimal art content this negative  description was turned into a positive  by minimalist artists they saw  minimalism as a kind of pure art to  quote the minimalist painter frank  stella what you see is what you see this  isn't art that copies something real a  person's face a nice horse or tries to  depict a feeling a minimalist art object  is itself and nothing else  all minimalism is in part a reaction in  the case of minimalist architecture it's  a reaction to decoration to ornament and  to fuss minimalist buildings are simple  and minimalist architects like Ludwig  Mies van der Rohe ER and mayor Lynn  create structures full of light and  space their work can be summed up in van  der Rohe s famous statement that less is  more minimalist gurus like Mary Kondo  believe in decluttering but say it's not  about knowing what to throw out it's  knowing what to keep a lot of minimalism  can appear harsh and inhuman the  exception is minimalistic music  pioneered by composers like Philip Glass  minimus music features repetitions  simple patterns and phase shifting the  movement of a repeating item to create  an arresting effect  despite the often austere simplicity of  the music or because of it many  minimalistic pieces of music are  profoundly moving and deeply emotional  minimalism is in part a reaction to the  increasingly busy and loud world around  us artists and consumers alike have  reacted against the  laughter and chaos of life and art and  created many disparate forms of  minimalism sometimes minimalism can seem  confusing as in Carl Andres famous brick  sculpture sometimes it can be stark like  a Mies van der or her office block but  sometimes as in the field of minimalist  music minimalism can be beautiful thanks  for watching don't forget to subscribe  and click the bail to receive  notifications for new videos see you  again soon
 

